{#- The one foot, on every page of the site and the app (design.md §12, 2026-09-28).

    There were two — the app's and the one the public pages wore — drawn by six
    stylesheets, and they had drifted into six slightly different rows of small links.
    Now one file and one stylesheet, carried inside the foot itself so no page can draw
    it differently: the lockup and what targum is, then targum and Follow at the far
    edge, then a line with the licence, the legal pages and, on a public page, the
    language. The Read column came out the same day (David, 2026-09-28).

    Expects `public` — true on the pages in front of the door, where the foot also
    offers the waitlist, Sign in and EN / RU; false inside the app, where the reader has
    an account and the desk's own menu says the language.

    Every link it draws is to a page that answers: the connector only while it is open,
    the legal pages only once they are published, the waitlist only while the front
    door is. -#}
{%- set public = public|default(false) %}
<style>{{ asset('foot.css') }}</style>
<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="sf-inner">
    <div class="sf-brand">
      <a class="sf-mark" href="/" aria-label="targum">
        <svg viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
          <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent, #a5824f)"></rect>
        </svg>
        targum
      </a>
      <p class="sf-tag">{{ t("landing.page.learn-modern-and-biblical-hebrew-from-videos-podcasts", "Learn modern and biblical Hebrew from videos, podcasts and books.") }}</p>
      {%- if public and front_door_is_open() %}
      <a class="sf-join" href="/#join">{{ t("landing.page.join-the-waitlist", "Join the waitlist") }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      {%- endif %}
      {#- Sign in under the waitlist (David, 2026-09-28): the two doors together, the one
          for somebody new first and the one for somebody who already has a key under it. -#}
      {%- if public %}
      <a class="sf-signin" href="/account/signin">{{ t("foot.sign-in", "Sign in") }}</a>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="sf-cols">
      <nav class="sf-col" aria-labelledby="sf-targum">
        {#- The name, as the name: lowercase and never translated (§6). -#}
        <p class="sf-head" id="sf-targum">targum</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/about">{{ t("foot.about", "About") }}</a></li>
          {#- The way into Claude and ChatGPT lives in the foot (design.md §12,
              2026-09-24): always true and rarely wanted. Named for what it does, "Install
              MCP", since 2026-09-28 (David); /connect still explains it for anybody who
              has never added one. -#}
          {%- if connector_is_open() %}
          <li><a href="/connect">{{ t("foot.install-mcp", "Install MCP") }}</a></li>
          {%- endif %}
          <li><a href="https://github.com/DLangellotti/targum">{{ t("foot.source", "Source") }}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
      {%- if social %}
      <nav class="sf-col" aria-labelledby="sf-follow">
        <p class="sf-head" id="sf-follow">{{ t("foot.follow", "Follow") }}</p>
        {#- targum's own accounts (`builder.SOCIAL`), as §7's glyphs: 16 units, a 1.4
            stroke, no fill — line drawings of the platforms' marks, never their colours
            (§10). The name is the label, and the title for a pointer. `rel="me"` says
            the account is this site's, for anyone checking. -#}
        <ul class="sf-social">
          {%- for name, address in social %}
          <li><a href="{{ address }}" rel="me" aria-label="{{ name }}" title="{{ name }}">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              {%- if name == 'X' %}
              <path d="M3 2.5h2.6l7.4 11h-2.6z"/><path d="M13 2.5 3 13.5"/>
              {%- elif name == 'Instagram' %}
              <rect x="2.5" y="2.5" width="11" height="11" rx="3.2"/><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="2.6"/><path d="M11.3 4.7h0"/>
              {%- elif name == 'LinkedIn' %}
              <rect x="2.5" y="2.5" width="11" height="11" rx="1.8"/><path d="M5.5 7.2v3.8M5.5 5h0M8 11V7.2M8 8.8c0-1.1.8-1.7 1.6-1.7s1.5.6 1.5 1.7V11"/>
              {%- else %}
              <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="5.5"/>
              {%- endif %}
            </svg>
          </a></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </nav>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sf-base">
    {#- The licence and the legal pages on one line, where a foot keeps them: privacy
        and terms rather than four legal links, since the schedule and the erasure
        procedure are one click on from privacy. -#}
    <p class="sf-small">
      <span>© 2026 targum · AGPL-3.0</span>
      {%- if legal_is_public() %}
      <a href="/privacy">{{ t("foot.privacy", "Privacy") }}</a>
      <a href="/terms">{{ t("foot.terms", "Terms") }}</a>
      {%- endif %}
    </p>
    {#- Two codes and a slash, as in the front door's bar: the one being read is ink,
        the other a link. `?lang=` on this same page, which is how every public page
        is addressed in another language (targum-internal#188). -#}
    {%- if public %}
    <p class="sf-tongue">
      {%- if page_language|default('en') == 'ru' %}<a href="?lang=en" lang="en">EN</a><span>/</span><b>RU</b>
      {%- else %}<b>EN</b><span>/</span><a href="?lang=ru" lang="ru">RU</a>{% endif %}
    </p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</footer>
